silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_4 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorTypedLegTaxonomyExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_4 silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliAnchorTypedLegTaxonomy', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, TypedLeg_taxonomy represents the taxonomy source leg as a typed olog object: the ITIS row TaxRow_TSN_183798 (Felis catus, rank Species, valid status) carrying the identification arrow lambda_tax into Mittens. The taxonomy leg is one of the ten cocone legs glue requires; it is preserved separately from the classification leg (DomesticCat) so the negative-regression \"Mittens = catus\" cannot fire.." .
